From: Producdevity <y.gherbi.dev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: backport QCA6390 helper and opt-in TTY attachment

Use btqca.c and btqca.h from Linux v5.10, commit
2c85ebc57b3e1817b6ce1a6b703928e113a90442, retaining the Linux Foundation
copyright and GPL-2.0-only license. Upstream source:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/tree/2c85ebc57b3e1817b6ce1a6b703928e113a90442/drivers/bluetooth

Keep the Neo3 vendor UART core. Its QCA protocol assumes serdev in three
TTY-reachable paths; use a guarded SoC selector and explicit qca6390_tty
parameter for the externally powered QCA6390. Default TTY mode remains ROME.
Adapt helper API calls and allow a version-only diagnostic that stops before
firmware download. Power control remains the caller's responsibility.

This diagnostic patch is excluded from the normal kernel patch set. Physical
acceptance currently covers signed module loading, UART ROM-version response,
power-state restoration and module unloading, not full Bluetooth operation.

